<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prussian War Academy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1810">1810</a>–<a href="/years/1919">1919</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Kriegsakademie</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Prussian War Academy (Kriegsakademie) in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> was founded in 1810 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gerhard-von-scharnhorst">Gerhard von Scharnhorst</a> to train officers for the general staff. Carl von Clausewitz was its director from 1818 to 1830, and under Moltke the Elder its graduates formed the general staff that won the wars of 1864–1871. It was closed under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-versailles">Treaty of Versailles</a> in 1919 and refounded in 1935.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prussian-war-academy.jpg" alt="Prussian War Academy" width="320" height="235" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Berlin_Kriegsakademie_Fassade_Unter_den_Linden.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
